From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: buffered animations, HitTestThemeBackground, IsCompositionActive (3713)

uxtheme: buffered animations, HitTestThemeBackground, IsCompositionActive

BeginBufferedAnimation, EndBufferedAnimation, BufferedPaintRenderAnimation
and BufferedPaintStopAllAnimations were stubs, so Explorer-style controls
that cross-fade their states never animated. An animation is two paint
buffers cross-faded over the duration (linear, cubic or sine) by a thread
timer that invalidates the area and the program's WM_PAINT; a zero
duration is a plain buffered paint. HitTestThemeBackground answers
HTNOWHERE/HTCLIENT for the rectangle or region and the sizing-border codes
for the HTTB_* options. IsCompositionActive reports DwmIsCompositionEnabled.
---
diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/Makefile.in b/dlls/uxtheme/Makefile.in
